 [{:title
   "Char-vs-byte span slicing silently drops or corrupts body text for any non-ASCII Markdown — demonstrated end-to-end: whole-document extraction failure",
   :file "src/epiphany/infra/adapters/lucene.clj",
   :detail
   "Spans recorded on extraction records are UTF-8 BYTE offsets (shape/markdown.clj:38-61 converts flexmark char offsets via char-offset->byte-offset), but two call sites slice with raw (subs s start end), which uses UTF-16 char offsets: (1) the new section-body-text introduced by this commit (lucene.clj:50-55) — its guard (<= 0 start end (count content)) compares byte offsets to a char count, so for non-ASCII docs it either returns nil (silent fallback to heading+path only, i.e. the exact story-03a bug this commit claims to fix) or slices shifted/garbage text; (2) the pre-existing but now production-reachable section-content-hash (section_extraction.clj:124-133, called from make-extraction-record:156) — it THROWS StringIndexOutOfBoundsException for non-ASCII docs, which extract-revision catches and records as a silent per-revision failure. End-to-end repro on this branch: a repo with u.md containing '# Café notes / The naïve zqxwvuniq body lives here.' -> 'ep ingest -p local' reports 'Sections extracted: 0, Extraction failures: 1' and exit 0; 'ep search zqxwvuniq --mode lexical' returns 0 results. REPL confirmation: body-span {:start-byte 9 :end-byte 26} vs (count blob)=24 -> subs(blob,9,26) throws 'Range [9, 26) out of bounds for length 24'. The correct slicer already exists and is unused here: epiphany.shape.markdown/slice (markdown.clj:269-274) does the byte->char conversion. The repo legislates Unicode exactness (AGENTS.md: '.ημ/ is a test case'); as delivered, any Markdown file containing a single non-ASCII character is entirely absent from the index with a success exit code.",
   :severity "blocker",
   :card "eng-003g",
   :lens "correctness",
   :survives true,
   :reasons
   ["Verified, not refuted. (1) Reproduced the throw at the REPL through the exact production chain: md/parse → extract-sections → make-extraction-record → section-content-hash on '# Café notes\\n\\nThe naïve zqxwvuniq body lives here.\\n' yields body-span {:start-byte 15 :end-byte 53} against a 51-char string and subs throws 'Range [15, 53) out of bounds for length 51'. (2) section_extraction.clj:130 slices with raw subs on byte offsets (spans are UTF-8 bytes via markdown.clj:38-61 char-offset->byte-offset); extract-revision (extraction_projection.clj:95-100) catches the StringIndexOutOfBoundsException and records only a per-revision failure while run-extraction-projection still reports :projection/completed true — so any non-ASCII doc vanishes from the index on a nominally successful run. (3) The second site, section-body-text at lucene.clj:50-55, is NEW code introduced by this card's commit fd20b30 and repeats the same bug: its guard (<= 0 start end (count content)) compares byte offsets to a UTF-16 char count, so it returns nil (silent fallback to heading+path — the exact story-03a regression the card claims to fix) or slices shifted garbage for docs where the hash happens not to throw. (4) The correct slicer epiphany.shape.markdown/slice (markdown.clj:269-274, byte->char conversion, tested at markdown_test.clj:147-155) exists and is unused at both sites. (5) Not deliberate/documented: the card's comment history records the story-03a fix, the tools.cli default fix, and the :local one-shot caveat, but says nothing about Unicode/byte-offset tradeoffs; repo law (AGENTS.md: '.ημ/ is a test case', exact path preservation byte-for-byte) legislates Unicode exactness. In scope because this card is what makes the throwing path production-reachable via ep ingest and itself added the second buggy slicer; the result — whole documents containing a single non-ASCII character silently absent from the index with exit 0 — defeats the card's core acceptance intent (ingest→search works end-to-end). Blocker severity stands."
    "Verified empirically on branch fd20b30 (this card's commit): created a fixture repo with u.md containing '# Café notes / The naïve zqxwvuniq body lives here.', ran `clojure -M:run -- ingest <repo> --profile local --index-dir <tmp>` — output: 'Sections extracted: 0, Extraction failures: 1', EXIT=0. `search zqxwvuniq --mode lexical` and even `search Caf` (the heading) return 0 results. The entire document is absent from the index with a success exit code. Code reading confirms the mechanism: (1) shape/markdown.clj:38-61 converts flexmark char offsets to UTF-8 BYTE offsets (:span/start-byte), so all recorded spans are byte offsets; (2) the NEW code this commit added, lucene.clj:45-55 section-body-text, slices with raw (subs content start end) — char-based — and its guard (<= 0 start end (count content)) compares byte offsets against a char count, so for non-ASCII docs it returns nil (silent fallback to heading+path, i.e. the exact story-03a bug this card's completion comment claims to fix) or slices shifted garbage; (3) grandfathered section-content-hash (section_extraction.clj:130) does the same raw subs and throws StringIndexOutOfBoundsException whenever the first section's body-span end-byte exceeds the char count, which extract-revision (extraction_projection.clj:95-100) catches and demotes to a per-revision failure — so the whole extraction record (and hence all indexing) is lost before section-body-text is even reached. Refutation angles all fail: not factually wrong (reproduced); not documented (card comments mention only the :local duplication caveat, nothing about Unicode/byte-vs-char); not out of scope (the card's core deliverable is 'ep ingest + durable Lucene search works end-to-end', its acceptance criterion is ingest-then-search returning the ingested section, and its own completion comment claims the body-text indexing fix — the new section-body-text is this commit's own defective code, and the card is precisely what makes the grandfathered hash bug production-reachable, per its Intent section: extraction was 'only reachable from tests' before); not minor (any Markdown file with a single non-ASCII character — utterly common prose — silently vanishes from the index with exit 0, while the repo legislates Unicode exactness in AGENTS.md). The correct slicer (shape.markdown/slice, markdown.clj:269-274) exists and is unused at both call sites. Real, in-scope, promotion-gating: blocker stands."]}
  {:title
   "ep ingest at its default profile (:services) always crashes registering any repo — repository-metadata-file/read! slurps a file that never exists",
   :file "src/epiphany/infra/main.clj",
   :detail
   "make-ingest-adapters wires the :services repository-metadata port as {:read repository-metadata-file/read! :write repository-metadata-file/write!} (main.clj:488-490). repository-metadata-file/read! (repository_metadata_file.clj:27-29) unconditionally slurps <common-git-dir>/corpus-archaeology/repository.edn; registration/register! calls :read before :write (registration.clj:22), so on any repo where the file does not yet exist read! throws FileNotFoundException and ingest exits 1 with 'Error: .../repository.edn (No such file or directory)'. Reproduced directly: (reg/register! {:git {...} :repository-metadata {:read rmf/read! :write rmf/write! ...} :observations ...} {:repository-path ...}) => THROWS java.io.FileNotFoundException. Worse, the file can never come into existence via the CLI: ep register --profile services (main.clj:134-136) and ep serve --profile services (main.clj:701-703) stub the metadata port with (fn [_] nil) reads/writes, and ingest's real write! is unreachable because read! throws first. So the default 'ep ingest <path>' invocation is broken for every repository, not just first-time ones. Fix: read! should return nil when the file is absent (analogous to the in-memory port), letting register! fall through to write!.",
   :severity "blocker",
   :card "eng-003g",
   :lens "correctness",
   :survives true,
   :reasons
   ["Claim verified by direct reproduction, not just code reading. (1) `ep ingest` defaults `--profile` to `:services` (main.clj:451-452) and `make-ingest-adapters` wires the real `repository-metadata-file/read!` (main.clj:488-489), which unconditionally slurps `<common-git-dir>/corpus-archaeology/repository.edn` (repository_metadata_file.clj:27-29). (2) `registration/register!` calls `:read` at line 21 and only reaches `:write` at line 34 when read returned nil — so on any repo lacking the file, read! throws first. Reproduced with the exact port functions the CLI wires: `(reg/register! {:repository-metadata {:read rmf/read! :write rmf/write! ...} ...} {:repository-path <fresh-repo>})` => `java.io.FileNotFoundException .../corpus-archaeology/repository.edn (No such file or directory)`; `run-ingest` catches it at main.clj:622 and exits 1 with exactly the error string the reviewer quotes. (3) The file is not created by the normal documented flow: `ep register --profile services` (main.clj:134-136) and `ep serve --profile services` (main.clj:701) stub the metadata port with `(fn [_] nil)`, so register-then-ingest at the default profile always crashes. (The claim's 'never via the CLI' is mildly overstated — `resolve-repository` in infra/repository_identity.clj does handle-missing-and-create, used by seed-candidate/inbox-decide — but ingest does not use it, so the core defect stands.) (4) In-scope and promotion-gating: this card's scope item 1 is literally the `ep ingest` subcommand with idempotent registration, its own completion note directs users to `:services` for incremental ingestion ('Use :services (MongoDB)... :local is one-shot/demo'), yet the only end-to-end test (ingest-local-then-lexical-search-finds-section, main_test.clj:233-237) exercises `-p local`; the default `:services` registration path is untested and broken for every fresh repository. No card comment documents this as an accepted tradeoff. The suggested fix (read! returns nil when absent, matching the in-memory port at in_memory.clj:38-39 and registration's `(when-not existing-metadata ...)` fallthrough) matches the evident design intent."
    "Reproduced the defect directly: (registration/register! ... {:repository-metadata {:read rmf/read! :write rmf/write!} ...}) on a fresh fixture repo throws java.io.FileNotFoundException for <common-git-dir>/corpus-archaeology/repository.edn. Code inspection confirms the chain: run-ingest (main.clj:578) calls register!, which calls (:read repository-metadata) before any :write (registration.clj:21,33-34); repository-metadata-file/read! (lines 27-29) slurps unconditionally with no existence check; ingest's default profile is :services (main.clj:452), which wires the real file adapter (main.clj:488-489). The file can never come into existence via the CLI because ep register --profile services (main.clj:134-136) and the pre-existing serve path stub the metadata port with (fn [_] nil) reads/writes, and ingest's own write! is unreachable since read! throws first. Refutation grounds all fail: (1) the claim is factually correct, verified by execution; (2) the behavior is not documented as a tradeoff — the card's IMPLEMENTED comment documents only a :local duplicate-docs caveat and actively recommends ':services (MongoDB) for incremental ingestion', i.e. the broken path; (3) it is squarely in scope — scope item 1 covers 'registers the repository (idempotent)' with ':services MongoDB' persistence, and git history shows this card's commit fd20b30 is the first ever to wire repository-metadata-file into a reachable production path (pre-fd20b30 main.clj stubbed the port everywhere), so the grandfathered read! became a live bug through this card's own wiring; (4) it is not minor — the headline feature's default invocation (ep ingest <path>) fails on every repository that has never been ingested, which is all of them; the acceptance-criteria unit test only exercised -p local, sidestepping the default profile. The suggested fix (read! returns nil when absent, matching the in-memory port's contract) is correct and small."]}
  {:title
   "ep ingest with default :services profile crashes on first run against a fresh repo — registration can never create repository.edn",
   :file "src/epiphany/infra/main.clj",
   :detail
   "make-ingest-adapters wires the REAL repository-metadata-file port for :services (`:read repository-metadata-file/read!`), but read! (src/epiphany/infra/repository_metadata_file.clj:27-29) slurps `<common-git-dir>/corpus-archaeology/repository.edn` unconditionally and throws java.io.FileNotFoundException when the file does not exist yet. registration/register! calls (:read repository-metadata) BEFORE the `(when-not existing-metadata ((:write ...)))` that would create the file, so first-ever registration via ingest is unreachable. Verified directly: `(reg/register! {:repository-metadata {:read mf/read! :write mf/write! ...}} ...)` on a fresh dir throws `java.io.FileNotFoundException \"/tmp/fresh-repo-git/corpus-archaeology/repository.edn (No such file or directory)\"`. Since ingest-options defaults `--profile` to :services (main.clj:453), the headline command `ep ingest <path>` fails in its default configuration on any never-registered repository; the raw IO exception also escapes the UNAVAILABLE/typed-error contract (caught only by the generic Exception handler). All ingest tests use `-p local` (test/epiphany/infra/main_test.clj:237), whose in-memory metadata port returns nil on first read, so the gap is untested. This commit is the first to wire repository-metadata-file into a CLI path (run-register :services still uses nil-returning stubs), so the violation is new. Violates the card's own scope item 1 ('registers the repository (idempotent)') and ADR-001's identity flow (first contact must mint + persist the resource-id). Fix: read! should return nil when the file is absent (or register! should tolerate the missing file).",
   :severity "blocker",
   :card "eng-003g",
   :lens "architecture-law",
   :survives true,
   :reasons
   ["Claim verified on every point by direct execution and code reading. (1) repository-metadata-file/read! (src/epiphany/infra/repository_metadata_file.clj:27-29) slurps unconditionally — reproduced: it throws java.io.FileNotFoundException when <common-git-dir>/corpus-archaeology/repository.edn is absent. (2) application/registration.clj:21 calls (:read repository-metadata) before the (when-not existing-metadata (:write ...)) at line 33, so a fresh repo can never reach the write — reproduced end-to-end: reg/register! with the real file adapters on a fresh common-git-dir throws FileNotFoundException. (3) make-ingest-adapters (main.clj:488) wires the real read!/write! only for :services, and ingest-options (main.clj:452) defaults --profile to :services, so the headline `ep ingest <path>` fails in its default configuration on any never-registered repository. (4) The raw FileNotFoundException escapes as a generic 'Error: ...' via the catch-Exception handler, not the typed UNAVAILABLE contract. (5) All ingest tests pass -p local (main_test.clj:228,237), whose in-memory metadata port returns nil on first read, so the gap is genuinely untested. (6) The card body/comment history contains no REVIEW/AUDIT disposition and no documented accepted tradeoff for this; the IMPLEMENTED note even recommends ':services (MongoDB) for incremental ingestion' — precisely the broken path. (7) The wiring into a CLI path is new in fd20b30 (this card's commit); run-register :services still uses nil-returning stubs (main.clj:134), so it is not grandfathered behavior. This is squarely within the card's scope item 1 ('registers the repository (idempotent)') and ADR-001's first-contact-mints-identity flow, and it gates the default invocation of the card's headline command — a real blocker, not refuted."
    "Every checkable element of the claim verifies against the actual code, and I reproduced the crash directly. (1) repository_metadata_file.clj:27-29 read! slurps <common-git-dir>/corpus-archaeology/repository.edn unconditionally — no .exists guard. (2) application/registration.clj:21 calls (:read repository-metadata) before the (when-not existing-metadata ... :write) at lines 33-34, so register!'s port contract expects read to return nil when absent (the in-memory adapter and run-register's stubs both honor that contract; the real file adapter violates it). (3) make-ingest-adapters (main.clj:488-490) wires the real mf/read! for :services, and ingest-options (main.clj:452) defaults --profile to :services. (4) Reproduced live: register! with the real ports against a fresh git repo threw java.io.FileNotFoundException on repository.edn. (5) There is no CLI workaround: run-register's :services branch (main.clj:134-136) uses {:read (fn [_] nil) :write (fn [_ _] nil)} stubs, so `ep register` never creates the file either — commit fd20b30 is indeed the first to wire repository-metadata-file into a CLI path. (6) The card's comment history does not document this as an accepted tradeoff; worse, the IMPLEMENTED note actively recommends ':services (MongoDB) for incremental ingestion' — the exact profile that crashes on first contact. Scope item 1 explicitly promises 'registers the repository (idempotent)' and ADR-001 requires first contact to mint+persist the resource-id, so this is squarely in delivered scope, and a headline command failing in its default configuration on every never-registered repository is promotion-gating, not minor. The raw FileNotFoundException also escapes via the generic Exception handler (main.clj:622), outside the typed-error contract."]}],
 :all
 [{:title
   "AC2's revision-at-path half has no direct test — only the extraction half does",
   :file "src/epiphany/infra/main.clj",
   :detail
   "Extraction idempotency is covered by run-extraction-projection-idempotent (extraction_projection_test.clj:117-139). Revision-at-path dedup lives in the private project-revision-at-path! (dedup via revision-at-path/observation-id-key against (:list-revision-at-path-by-resource observations)); the only supporting test is observation-id-key stability (revision_at_path_test.clj:255). No test re-runs the projection helper or the CLI to show zero new revision-at-path observations. The dedup logic is simple and correct on inspection, but the acceptance criterion names both record types and only one is demonstrated by a test.",
   :severity "nit",
   :card "eng-003g",
   :lens "dod-coverage",
   :survives false,
   :reasons
   ["The finding is self-labeled 'nit' and concedes the dedup logic is correct on inspection — by definition it is not promotion-gating. Substantively, the pieces ARE tested: revision_at_path_test.clj covers observation-id-key stability plus three dedup tests (deduplicate-removes-identical-observations, -keeps-distinct, -preserves-first-occurrence, lines 244-280), and main.clj's project-revision-at-path! is a thin composition of those tested domain functions over the observations port's list operation. The claim demands a test that re-runs the CLI/projection helper, but the card's own completion record documents why that is not a unit-testable path: ':local ingest caveat: observations are in-memory, so a second :local ingest re-extracts... Use :services (MongoDB) for incremental ingestion; :local is one-shot/demo. Known limitation, documented in --help.' A true CLI re-run idempotency test requires MongoDB, i.e. the integration suite, while the card's declared verification is ['unit-test'] — so the demanded test is outside the card's delivered scope. The acceptance criterion's idempotency mechanism (identity keys) is demonstrated; the residual gap is an integration-level re-run test, not a unit-test defect, and too minor to gate review→done."
    "The claim is directionally accurate but not promotion-gating, and its own severity is 'nit'. The dedup mechanism it questions is not untested: the identity-key contract it depends on is directly covered — observation-id-key stability and the deduplicate semantics (removes-identical, keeps-distinct, preserves-first-occurrence) are tested in revision_at_path_test.clj:244-280, and project-revision-at-path! in main.clj:496-527 is a thin, pure remove-by-identity-key over those tested primitives. More importantly, the missing re-run test cannot be a unit test at all: with :local profile observations are in-memory, so a second ingest has no prior observations to dedup against — the card's own IMPLEMENTED comment documents this as a known, accepted limitation ('Use :services (MongoDB) for incremental ingestion; :local is one-shot/demo'). Demonstrating revision-at-path re-run idempotency therefore requires a live MongoDB, i.e. the integration suite, which this repo explicitly treats as environment-gated (exits UNAVAILABLE without services) and which already carries 2 pre-existing baseline failures. The card's declared verification is unit-test, AC2's mechanism is demonstrated at the domain level for both record types (extraction re-run test plus revision-at-path identity-key/dedup tests), and the residual gap is integration-scope, documented, and self-labeled a nit — none of which should gate a review→done promotion."]}
  {:title
   "ep ingest --embed is not idempotent even under :services — re-running duplicates KNN embedding docs in the durable index",
   :file "src/epiphany/infra/main.clj",
   :detail
   "embed-extractions! lists ALL recorded section extractions for the resource and calls (:embed-sections! ...) then (:index-embeddings! ...) unconditionally on every run. The Lucene adapter's :index-embeddings! (lucene.clj:229-236) only ever calls .addDocument — there is no delete/update-by-key and no dedup against previously indexed vectors. So under :services (where revision-at-path and extraction records ARE correctly deduped, making re-ingest the supported incremental path), a second `ep ingest --embed` re-embeds every section and appends a duplicate KNN doc per section to the durable index, producing duplicated semantic/hybrid results. The card's documented one-shot limitation covers only :local section-doc duplication; this affects the :services path the card designates as incremental, and conflicts with AGENTS.md's 'retry must not duplicate anything' rule. Not covered by AC2's wording (which names only revision-at-path observations and extraction records) but it is the same durable-command-retry contract. No test exercises a second --embed run.",
   :severity "should-fix",
   :card "eng-003g",
   :lens "dod-coverage",
   :survives false,
   :reasons
   ["The code characterization is accurate (lucene.clj :index-embeddings! at lines 229-236 only calls .addDocument with no delete/update-by-key, and main.clj embed-extractions! lines 530-543 re-lists all recorded extractions and re-embeds unconditionally on every --embed run), but the finding fails on scope and documentation grounds. (1) The card's own 'Out of scope' section explicitly defers exactly this concern: 'Embedding projection checkpoints/resumability (extraction projection already checkpoints; embeddings are re-derivable).' Incremental re-embed dedup is the same deferral — the card deliberately treats embeddings as re-derivable rather than incrementally maintained. (2) ADR-000 (architecturally authoritative, cards never override it) states Lucene/vector projections are rebuildable and 'a cache or index is never the only copy of a fact or decision' — the adapter even ships :rebuild-index!/:clear-index! for exactly this. Duplicate KNN docs in a rebuildable projection are not durable-fact duplication; the AGENTS.md 'retry must not duplicate anything' rule governs durable identity/observation records, which AC2 covers and which ARE deduped (project-revision-at-path! lines 496-528 dedups by observation-id-key; the extraction projection skips already-processed revisions per extraction_projection.clj:140). (3) The claimed user impact is bounded: worst case is the same section appearing twice in top-k semantic results until an index rebuild, requiring Ollama plus a deliberate second --embed run — a quality wart on an explicitly-deferred capability, not a correctness violation of any acceptance criterion. This belongs in a follow-up card on incremental embedding projection, not as a gate on review→done for a card whose ACs (observation/extraction idempotency, durable lexical search, UNAVAILABLE-on-Ollama-down) are demonstrably met."
    "The code reading is accurate — embed-extractions! (main.clj:530-543) re-embeds ALL recorded extractions and lucene.clj:229-236 :index-embeddings! only ever calls .addDocument, so a second `ep ingest --embed` under :services does append duplicate KNN docs. But the finding is refuted on scope and authority grounds. (1) The card's own 'Out of scope' section explicitly defers exactly this concern: 'Embedding projection checkpoints/resumability (extraction projection already checkpoints; embeddings are re-derivable).' Dedup-on-rerun for embeddings IS the resumability/checkpointing concern — the implementer documented that embeddings are re-derivable and deliberately did not build skip-already-embedded logic. (2) AGENTS.md's 'retry must not duplicate anything' rule lives under 'Identity & idempotency' and governs durable facts/decisions; the same document's Data authority section (ADR-000) states 'Lucene/vector/graph projections are rebuildable — a cache or index is never the only copy of a fact or decision.' Duplicate KNN docs in a rebuildable projection are repairable by deleting the index dir and re-ingesting; no canonical fact is corrupted. (3) AC2 names revision-at-path observations and extraction records, both of which ARE deduped under :services as required; the embedding side was never in the acceptance criteria. (4) The add-only :index-embeddings! adapter behavior predates this card (story-03a, git log confirms lucene.clj's embedding path is grandfathered; this card only touched section->doc for the body-text bug). A duplicated-embedding-rows-in-a-rebuildable-cache issue, explicitly deferred by the card and violating no durable-fact contract, does not gate a review→done promotion; it belongs on a follow-up embedding-projection card."]}
